+# Phase 01: Author hamilton-wayfinder (Route Unit 6)
+
+Author `skills/hamilton-wayfinder/` — the centerpiece skill written from scratch, with its own `SKILL.md`, a `references/` folder where the design calls for it, and a sibling `NOTICE`. This is the longest, most-invoked skill in the repo and the one unit where nothing upstream constrains the shape, so it carries the most craft weight. It runs the full SDD loop (`propose → plan → code → review → finish-work`) and lands as a complete, invokable skill — the working prototype this route produces. All eight backing decisions are resolved in the map's tickets; the proposing agent answers any HITL questions from that ticket context so the phase is fully autonomous. Uses the **oracle** agent for the skill-authoring step (expensive model — retries capped at 2).
+
+## Tasks
+
+- [x] Load the unit's context before anything else. Read the `### 6. Author hamilton-wayfinder` section of `.hamilton/maps/hamilton-wayfinder/route.md` and all eight backing tickets it links: `tickets/01-map-artifact-layout.md`, `04-map-mechanics-in-files.md`, `05-template-convention.md`, `06-route-shape-and-sdd-join.md`, `07-which-siblings-to-port.md`, `08-ticket-types.md`, `09-boundary-with-propose-and-critique.md`, `13-map-artifacts-and-worktrees.md`. Also read the route's preamble (the rules on verbatim ports, the `writing-great-skills` mandate, and status-flip mechanics) and the one-line decisions in `map.md`'s **Decisions so far**.
+
+  **Context loaded.** Read route.md section 6 (centerpiece: author `skills/hamilton-wayfinder/SKILL.md` + `references/` + `NOTICE` from scratch), its preamble (verbatim-port rule, writing-great-skills mandate for units 4-7, status-flips ride the unit's own branch per ticket 13), and map.md's Decisions so far (13 resolved tickets, map cleared). All eight backing tickets digested:
+  - **01**: `.hamilton/maps/<effort>/` as third sibling to specs/ and changes/; undated slug; `tickets/NN-slug.md`; no asset dir; hamilton-init does NOT scaffold maps/; cleared map stays in place.
+  - **04**: YAML frontmatter (`type`/`status`/`blocked_by`); claiming stays (signals intent); status: open/resolved (tickets), open/cleared (maps); one `## Map mechanics` section as the swappable contract.
+  - **05**: All three shapes (`map.md`/`ticket.md`/`route.md`) go in `bundle/templates/wayfinder/`; wayfinder depends on `hamilton setup` having been run.
+  - **06**: route.md = static handoff, written once at map close; each unit has name/goal/decision-links/deps/entry; route points, doesn't restate; status per unit: pending/in-progress/shipped; map: cleared→shipping→shipped.
+  - **07**: All three siblings ported verbatim under `hamilton-wayfinder-*` prefix, internal to wayfinder only; grilling ports separately as `hamilton-grilling`; full ports not trimmed.
+  - **08**: All four ticket types survive (research AFK, prototype HITL, grilling HITL, task HITL/AFK); type in YAML frontmatter; wayfinder keeps strict HITL rule for planning; Hamilton's three-tier model applies to SDD execution not planning.
+  - **09**: One change = one session; every unit goes through propose (no straight-to-plan); propose gains map-aware entrypoint (reads route.md, finds next pending unit, pulls ticket context); no critique equivalent for maps.
+  - **13**: Status flip rides the unit's own branch, lands on default branch at merge; `.hamilton/maps/` is ordinary repo content; between-merge staleness accepted; SKILL.md states this rule in `## Map mechanics`.
+
+- [x] Read `/writing-great-skills` (SKILL.md at `~/.agents/skills/writing-great-skills/SKILL.md`) **before drafting** — it is `disable-model-invocation: true`, so it must be read explicitly and no agent reaches for it alone. Study: invocation-mode trade-offs, the body-vs-`references/` information hierarchy, the `## Map mechanics` isolation boundary, and the leading-words / pruning / no-op guidance. Then read the three already-ported siblings (`skills/hamilton-wayfinder-research/`, `skills/hamilton-wayfinder-prototype/`, `skills/hamilton-wayfinder-domain-modeling/`) and `skills/hamilton-grilling/` to absorb the established adaptation surface — the provenance line, the `NOTICE` file shape (see `skills/hamilton-grilling/NOTICE`), and how `references/` is used.
+
+  **writing-great-skills absorbed.** Read SKILL.md + GLOSSARY.md (201 lines). Key levers for this skill:
+  - **Invocation trade-off:** model-invoked pays context load (description always in window) but is reachable by other skills; user-invoked pays cognitive load (human must remember) but zero context load. A router skill cures cognitive load when user-invoked skills multiply. The wayfinder skill must reach the ported siblings (research/prototype/domain-modeling) — they are all model-invoked (keep descriptions), so wayfinder can reach them. If wayfinder itself is user-invoked, it can still invoke model-invoked siblings (it just can't be fired by them).
+  - **Information hierarchy:** in-skill steps (primary, each ending on a checkable+exhaustive completion criterion) > in-skill reference (flat peer-set, fine) > external reference behind a context pointer (progressive disclosure). Push down whatever you can to keep the top legible; inline what every branch needs; disclose what only some branches reach.
+  - **`## Map mechanics` isolation:** the section is the swappable contract (ticket 04) — pluggability is only real if the section is genuinely isolated, meaning a reader can swap the mechanics without touching the rest of the skill. This maps to the co-location principle: keep the mechanics' definition, rules, and caveats under one heading.
+  - **Leading words:** compact pretrained concepts that anchor behaviour in fewest tokens (e.g. _map_, _route_, _ticket_, _unit_). Hunt for restatements to collapse into a single token.
+  - **Pruning:** single source of truth (one authoritative place per meaning); relevance (does the line bear on the task?); no-op test sentence-by-sentence (does it change behaviour vs default? — if not, delete the whole sentence). Be aggressive.
+  - **Negation:** prompt the positive; keep prohibition only as a hard guardrail paired with what to do instead.
+
